  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your disguise is garish or daringly fashionable. While you wear this disguise, other creatures who can see you have a +2 circumstance bonus on saving throws against pattern effects, gaze attacks, and other visual effects that do not originate from you and take a –2 penalty on Perception checks to notice anything other than you. You also gain a +4 circumstance bonus on skill checks to impress someone, create a diversion with Bluff, pose a menace with Intimidate, or entertain. If you create a diversion with Bluff and choose yourself as the object, you can use your Disguise modifier in place of your Bluff modifier and the distraction lasts until the end of your next turn.</p>\n<p>Your disguise imposes a –4 penalty on Stealth checks and ensures anyone who sees you remembers you.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/subterfuge#toc30\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
